From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lycaos <caraboune@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 22:57:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] session-agent: open a session on a chosen agent from inside
 the TUI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The agent a session runs on is decided when the session is created: the
pager stamps `_meta.agentProfile` and the shell prefers it over
`[agent] name` and `GROK_AGENT`. That field was only ever filled from
`--agent` at launch, so picking an agent meant restarting the process —
and the agents modal, which is where you actually read definitions,
could not act on one.

`/agent <name>` (alias `/use-agent`) sets the same field and opens a new
session on it. A new session rather than a conversion of the current one,
because the agent is fixed at creation; saying so is more honest than
pretending to switch in place.

Gork-Patch-Id: session-agent
Gork-Risk: low
